WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.320
Shrieka? Where are you, baby?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.040
You know, they say it's the
last free place in America.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.560
And it is, for people that
live here year round.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.720
People got places they can
stay, and they're safe.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:46.120
We do have name streets, we do have
neighborhoods, like a normal city.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.600
But we're not paying land rent.
We could never pay land rent here.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.200
What do I need a city for?
Can just live out here, for free.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:10.360
If Palm Springs and Deadwood, South
Dakota would have an illegitimate child -

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.520
it would be Slab City.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:18.560
And that's Deadwood, South
Dakota of 1876, not today.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.960
Shrieka?

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.040
Oh, Shrieka?
Where are you, baby?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.680
Shrieka!

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.840
Dammit dog, where are you?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.880
My name is Robert Lane.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:03:00.000
I came down here two and a half
years ago to visit my best friend.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:07.040
And he wanted to trade
his place for my truck.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.280
After thinking about it for
a day, I decided to stay.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.840
So he took my truck
and I got a home.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.640
I always start off with
my home town news,

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.120
even though I haven't been
there in nearly 3 years.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.120
It's nice to be able to know what's
going on in other parts of the world.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:35.520
To know that people are the same everywhere.
They all have the same worries and concerns that we do.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.880
Color of our skin
doesn't mean shit.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:11.400
You fuck around with children, or threaten
children, you're gonna see my dark side.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.040
I even trained my dogs to protect
the children around here.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:26.640
Last week somebody had every last
possession they owned stolen or burnt.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.520
It's what's known
as Slab justice.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.680
He was...

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.280
He was a real asshole.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:36.000
He went to jail two weeks ago
for threatening somebody,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.440
and within 24 hours of
him being in jail -

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.880
all of his stuff was stolen
and burned to the ground.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.480
Nobody called the police when
the fire was immediately set.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:02.960
They waited 'til it was inextinguishable
before calling the fire department.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.880
That's how hated
this person was.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.720
So... There are morals out
here, they're just different.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:29.160
A lot of people have put a lot of taboo about it.
But it's just like any other neighborhood,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:36.280
any other city, any of that you'd find
here in the US, as far as I know.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.000
Where is that bag?

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.280
- What bag?
- Our shit.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.400
It's the same thing to me, man.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.880
If somebody took my fuckin' travel bag,
I'm gonna beat the shit out of 'em.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.120
Where's my bag?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.640
If there's a fuckin' Black Widow there,
don't be puttin' your goddamn hand down there.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.200
No, Black Widow's right there.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.480
- Have you seen my green duffel bag?

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.440
- It's right here, Bro.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.640
You just get the wrong
impression, you know.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.200
I mean, if I looked at somebody like this,
that looked like me, I don't think I would trust him.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.720
But I'm the most trustworthy
person you'll ever find.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.760
You give me a thousand dollars
to hold for ya for six months,

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.320
when you come back, you
might get 999 dollars back.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:35.600
I might have spent a dollar on some
bubble gum that I can't chew.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.800
Fuckin' buried.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.600
The wind stopped blowin'.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.640
Life is good out here.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.600
Some hippies do shave.
Not very many, but some.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.440
I own a place called the
Slab City Internet Cafe.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:02.960
The only public place in town for internet,
electricity and, in the mornings, coffee.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.480
The coffee situation...

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.080
It's interesting, he
don't even like coffee.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:21.080
I can't stand the crap. It's the
nastiest tasting stuff I've ever tried.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.960
And I tried it twice
just to make sure.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.360
He has never drank coffee,
he's gonna live longer than us.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.760
I can't even stand
the smell of it.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.640
The smell turns my stomach.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:40.200
But my customers like coffee, so I
give them coffee in the morning.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.920
He taught me how to
make it his way.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.120
Can you carry this one out?

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.280
Holy shit.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.000
Holy fuckballs!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.560
Fuck shopping malls!

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.480
So great. Java loves us!

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.400
So good!

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.240
My day usually
starts pretty early.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.400
The wintertime, I'll start
coffee about 6 o'clock in the morning

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.640
to get coffee out for
the customers by 7.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.080
I wouldn't know if I make
good coffee or bad,

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.320
but I've been told I make
the best cup in the county.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.760
Gobbles a lot of coffee in your mouth
before you even try to take a sip.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:39.040
I do coffee from 7 'til 10 or 7 'til 11,
depending on how many people are around.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.560
I'm open 7 days a week.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:50.120
I don't have coffee all day long,
because they could drink me dry.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh! I wasn't blocking!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:34.480
I run strictly solar but
I have enough power

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.000
coming off my panels that I
can provide electricity -

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:44.200
up until maybe 2 hours
before sundown.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.080
I have no power, no
lights, no nothing.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:55.280
This place - you can take your cell
phone, you can plug it into a power cord,

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.200
you can charge it up, you can
do that with your computer too.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.400
And if you've got people you
wanna keep in touch with,

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.840
you can get online, which
seems to be pretty unique.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:11.680
I think he's got 6 or 8 batteries over
there and a 1000 watts of solar power -

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:14.280
so the people can come
in there and plug in.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:21.320
All he is asking is for donations so
he can pay for some of that stuff.

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:23.320
Rob's one of my best friends.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.600
The cafe has always been
like a home for me.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:31.480
A home away from home.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.720
It's probably one of my
favorite places to hang out.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.960
Pretty fuckin' awesome.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:46.360
It's a community, it's
like a small neighborhood.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:50.880
Everybody out here is pretty much like
family. Not everybody, but most of us.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.480
Damn, it's already 11 o'clock.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.680
God, this morning's gone quick!

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.240
Hey Charlie!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.240
Come here, baby.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.800
Shrieka!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.320
Oh, Shrieka...

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.160
Shrieka!

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:46.960
Damn that dog.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.600
Shrieka!

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:53.840
Come on!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:04.680
It took a little while to get used to the
heat, but it definitely beats the cold.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.040
Less than 300 people live
here during the summer.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:14.600
Wintertime, there could be
as many as 2000 people here.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.480
But come June and
the real heat -

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:22.480
they're all gone.
You're talking just...

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:27.480
Just the people who can
tolerate extreme heats.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.680
Which is a very hard thing to do for a
lot of people, that come out without -

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.320
the knowledge or understanding
of this desert.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.760
Because it does get very
very hot in the summer.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.600
125 degrees, 130 degrees.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.160
We're talking 50-55 degrees Celsius,
for people who can't convert.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.880
When it gets up to 125 degrees...

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:08.760
I hardly ever drink during the summer,
because the alcohol dehydrates you.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:16.040
So I do all my drinking
when it's cool.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.960
Get my belly ready
for the summer.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.960
- I'm not going anywhere ever.
- No, in your mind?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:08.560
Oh, in my mind? Oh no, in my
brain, I'm here, waiting on a bus.

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.120
I'm here, waiting on a couple
of buses and the president.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:13.760
But that's never gonna happen.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.520
But that's OK... Sit around,
waiting, patiently.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.680
I randomly found my
way to Slab City.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.000
I was on my way to my
friend's court case in LA -

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:34.040
and we ran into a friend that
mentioned Slab City,

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:37.840
so we made the way here,
we rented a BMW -

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:41.320
and that car blew up, we traded
it for a van, that blew up...

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.160
And we finally
made our way here.

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:48.640
I was travelling through when people were talking
about this free place to live in the winter.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:54.240
We came out here to check it out.
I fell in love with the place.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:59.200
I was like a snowbird, I would come
down every winter over to Arizona.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:02.480
While I was camped there,
two ladies came up and said,

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:06.200
"George, you ever been to Slab
City?" "No, I've heard of it..."

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.400
"But I've never been there."

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:13.040
"Oh, God, you gotta go there, you'd fit right
in, you'd fit right in to Slab City life."

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:18.080
Snowbird is a type of person
who runs away from the cold -

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.320
kind of like I did.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.720
But they only come
down for the winter,

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.400
and then as soon as the weather
starts to warm up -

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.760
they'll go back north to
where they came from.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.440
I decided to change
my life around.

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.440
Be wild, and...

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.120
Do the things they told me I couldn't do
when I was teenager and all that other stuff -

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:49.320
rebel against society
and everything.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:54.520
Got myself in legal troubles that
sent me to prison for 7 years.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:17:00.200
And, in the last year, I've
just gotten out of prison.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.040
There is no hostility.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:09.640
I don't think there's a single person
here that hates another person at all.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.120
It's been amazing.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:18.920
It's been a long time since I felt
this accepted in a random environment.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:25.960
Now, I'm starting over my life
as a single, elderly lady.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:32.280
Payed my debt to the society and
got out and came down here.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:37.080
I hadn't intended on
staying permanently...

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:43.160
There is a lot of quiet
moments, which is nice...

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:46.280
I spent a lot of time in a big
city, I enjoy the big city,

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.360
but I also like the peace
and quiet of the country.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:31.520
Just coming here has
really changed me -

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:34.720
in multiple ways:
mentally, physically...

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:40.160
Before I got here I was, honestly,
just hurting other people and myself.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:45.840
And now I've come to the realization
of who I am and what I'm worth...

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:49.200
I have Slab City and the
people here to thank for that.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.560
Come here!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:53.880
Now.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:11.240
There are no public
utilities out here, so...

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.960
If you need water, you have
to obtain it for yourself.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:19.480
You don't pay rent but you still pay.
You gotta pay for water.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.640
You gotta pay for your food.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.600
You gotta pay for your
clothing and the laundry.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:27.520
The upkeep on your dog.
The upkeep on your place.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:31.800
You gotta pay for that and you gotta find
a way to do it out here the best you can.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:40.000
One tank is between 270 and 300 gallons
of water. That usually lasts 3-4 weeks.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:41.400
- George?

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:45.560
One of the great things about my place
is that I'm the only one out here -

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:50.360
that's got a shower that's
got a hot water tank on it.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.880
Everybody stops by and
I gotta help 'em.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:20:00.160
It's not really a public shower. You do
gotta come over and ask permission, but -

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:04.440
George is a nice enough guy that
most people, he will say "yes" to.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.160
People come by and I charge
'em 3 dollars for a shower.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.880
'Cause I've gotta burn my propane.
And then the water...

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.000
I gotta run in and
haul my water, so...

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.480
3 bucks is pretty cheap.

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:20.480
You have to be very conservative
with your water out here.

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:23.360
If you take a shower, you
take a trickle shower.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:29.280
You wet yourself down, turn the water off,
soap yourself up, turn the water back on -

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:30.960
rince yourself off.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:38.400
You flip a light switch and it turns
the pump on. And you take your shower.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:44.800
If you could do a shower
in less than 5 gallons -

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.520
that just means you've got
shower water for another day.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:50.760
Don't use it during my TV time!

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.280
It's pretty cool.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.680
You look so much better!

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.280
I bet you smell better too.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:10.800
I feel pretty... Oh, so pretty.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.240
Yeah, well, you don't
look any better!

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:23.360
I give him showers for free.
That's how good of a friend it is.

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:26.360
Like it costs 3 dollars
to be my friend.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.160
A good day for me is a slight breeze
outside with a nice sunshine

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:58.200
so I can go outside and
do my normal activities.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:12.040
I live out here in Slab
City because it's awesome.

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:18.480
I've three older brothers
and one sister. 4 dogs.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:24.880
I work out here every Saturday, picking
up garbage off the side of the road.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:28.160
There is no more jobs
out here to do -

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:34.040
except being a gas station
worker or food market worker.

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:45.840
During the week I go to school and
basically do nothing except school stuff.

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:51.160
Then I just go home
and do my homework.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:53.120
Well, supposedly do my homework.

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:55.800
And... That's about it.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:17.480
I am still hoping to be able
to go to the moon one day.

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:24.760
I'm serious. I've been
wanting to go to the moon

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:29.080
since Neil Armstrong touched
down on the moon in 1969.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.480
I may not be able to
travel to another star, but...

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:38.000
In 5-10 years I could
very well stand on the moon.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:40.680
And I would love that!

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:47.120
I wanna be like a soldier in
the US Army or Air Force...

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:49.760
Somewhere around there,
when I grow up.

00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:53.680
Because, I wanna just
hear gun battles -

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:57.600
and see what it's really like
instead of video games and movies.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:06.040
On the other side of the fence, off
of Canal Road here in Slab City -

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.040
we have 3 military bases.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.040
We've got the Marines, the
Air Force and the Naval.

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:15.960
And everyone once in a while you
get the airplanes going over,

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.440
you get the bombs going off,

00:24:17.440 --> 00:24:19.480
you get the firing...

00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:21.520
Test sites is what it is.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:26.080
It makes it quite loud if
you're not used to it,

00:24:26.080 --> 00:24:29.520
but you get used to it when
you're out here long enough.

00:24:30.200 --> 00:24:34.840
Once in a while you'll see a cloud of smoke
rise up off of the top of the mountain -

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:39.280
and then like 10 seconds later,
you'll hear this... BOOM!

00:24:39.320 --> 00:24:42.240
The cloud of smoke will already be there,
you're just hearing it afterwards.

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:43.440
It's like... Delayed.

00:24:57.960 --> 00:25:02.000
I like seeing the helicopters
fly over our heads...

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.680
What they mainly do in the morning is go
really really low and really really loud.

00:25:16.760 --> 00:25:19.520
They're not supposed
to wave at us.

00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:22.720
About a month ago, there
was three of 'em -

00:25:22.760 --> 00:25:25.080
they were flying
real' low over here.

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:27.680
And I stood out here with
a beer, waving at 'em.

00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:29.840
And somebody hung out the
door and waved back.

00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:32.080
I don't know if they got
in trouble for it or not,

00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:35.240
but that was the
first time in 2.5 years -

00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:37.760
anybody had ever waved back.

00:25:37.840 --> 00:25:41.080
Yeah, made me feel pretty good.
They saw me.

00:26:19.720 --> 00:26:24.800
You know how you send around
notes in classes and shit...

00:26:24.800 --> 00:26:27.120
We're passing around notes
and Miss Reed comes around:

00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:28.640
"Listen, Mr Fields.

00:26:28.680 --> 00:26:31.040
What are you doin' passin' around notes
while I'm trying to teach a class?"

00:26:31.040 --> 00:26:34.240
- I'm like: "Well... I'm bored."
- Bored as fuck.

00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:38.800
And she was like: "You can leave this
classroom right now and get suspended" -

00:26:38.800 --> 00:26:41.000
"or you could stay in this
classroom and go to detention."

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.920
I'm like: "Miss Reed, you're my
favorite teacher, I love science."

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:47.240
"But if you give me
detention, I'm not goin'."

00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:50.840
I'd say I'm kind of a greeter
but I'm kind of family too.

00:26:51.120 --> 00:26:55.120
A bunch of the kids like to talk
to me and hang around with me.

00:26:55.120 --> 00:27:00.400
I'm saying kids like half my age.
20-year-olds.

00:27:00.400 --> 00:27:02.080
They adopt me as "Mom".

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:04.120
I was thinking to myself:
why do I have detention?

00:27:04.120 --> 00:27:06.560
I haven't done anything wrong!

00:27:06.560 --> 00:27:10.200
So you know what I did?
I stopped doin' all of my work.

00:27:10.200 --> 00:27:11.240
I didn't do fuckin' shit.

00:27:11.240 --> 00:27:13.320
I went to the class and
I put my head down.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:16.120
They won't say it out
loud or anything else,

00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:19.480
but there is a couple of 'em
that look at me like Mom.

00:27:20.160 --> 00:27:21.720
I kind of fit into that role.

00:27:21.720 --> 00:27:27.360
I've had five kids. My youngest
is 21, my oldest is 30.

00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:30.680
I got four grandkids.
Haven't seen any of 'em.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:34.600
So it finally came to the point
where I met the principal.

00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:38.320
So I'm sitting here like this, sleeping on
my desk, and this motherfucker comes in -

00:27:38.320 --> 00:27:40.960
takes that big-ass fuckin'
textbook off the table...

00:27:42.440 --> 00:27:46.040
Fuckin'... He didn't hit
the table, he hit me!

00:27:46.040 --> 00:27:50.000
I jumped off that chair and fuckin' knocked
him one right in his fuckin' mouth!

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:54.840
Well, Zack is my brother.
Personally, that dude is funny.

00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:58.600
I like waking up and Zack is right
there and knowin' that I got a brother

00:27:58.960 --> 00:28:00.080
that's with me right now.

00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:02.600
Bitches!

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:08.880
My brother was killed
by the law enforcement,

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.520
and my cousin was killed
because of gangs.

00:28:12.920 --> 00:28:14.360
I miss them.

00:28:14.440 --> 00:28:15.920
So much.

00:28:16.720 --> 00:28:17.680
I miss 'em.

00:28:18.360 --> 00:28:20.320
I was flippin' the fuck out.

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:25.280
I'm not allowed on any public
school grounds in California.

00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:26.440
Ever.

00:28:27.800 --> 00:28:28.920
EVER.

00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:30.440
Zack is my guy.

00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:33.200
He is cool, man. He helped me
out when I first came here.

00:28:33.200 --> 00:28:37.560
He was like: "You! I like you!" And
I'm like: "I like you too, Bro."

00:28:37.560 --> 00:28:39.000
We've been cool ever since.

00:28:50.080 --> 00:28:52.240
Did you take my cigarette?

00:28:52.240 --> 00:28:53.240
Yup.

00:28:54.880 --> 00:28:57.800
Man, I can have
nothing around here.

00:29:00.080 --> 00:29:01.560
You know Casey and Timmie?

00:29:01.680 --> 00:29:05.440
My older brother taught 'em that it was cool to
run up to me as fast and as hard as they could -

00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:07.640
powerslide, and punch
me in the balls.

00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:10.800
I can't have any more kids
besides the one I have,

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:13.960
and I don't feel anything if you
punch me in the testicles.

00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:15.680
So, good luck!

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:19.400
You don't feel pain in your testicles,
I don't feel pain in this foot.

00:29:19.400 --> 00:29:23.080
'Cause I've been kicked in it so many times, 'cause
everybody keep thinkin' that's my weak spot.

00:29:23.080 --> 00:29:26.120
No, buddy! It's actually
my strong spot.

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:30.080
All through my life people thought
that because I walk like this,

00:29:30.120 --> 00:29:31.880
that foot is my weakness.

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:33.840
At one time, it used to be.

00:29:33.840 --> 00:29:38.160
But so many people have tried to kick me in
there... Actually have kicked me in there -

00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:40.360
that I felt pain when
it first started.

00:29:40.360 --> 00:29:45.200
But I'm just so used to gettin' kicked
there. Doesn't mind it no more.

00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:48.320
And I'm gonna do to you what I would do
to anybody else that throws a kick at me,

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:49.280
I'm gonna grab your foot...

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:52.480
- You think you're invincible?
- I'm not invincible, but I'm gonna grab that foot...

00:29:52.480 --> 00:29:54.840
- That's what you're thinkin'.
- So let's go out there and test the theory -

00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:56.120
or it can get dropped right now.

00:29:56.120 --> 00:29:58.680
- You wanna go test that theory?
- Yes.

00:30:03.120 --> 00:30:05.160
I won't put you to sleep,
but you will tap.

00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:08.120
I love music.

00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:10.480
Actually, I am a beat creator.

00:30:10.480 --> 00:30:13.000
I have been making beats
since I was young.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:17.520
Started gettin' good, everybody recognized it, it was
like: "You're doin' good, man, you should keep goin'!"

00:30:17.520 --> 00:30:19.040
Okay. Kept goin'.

00:30:20.840 --> 00:30:22.520
You can hear one of
my instrumentals.

00:30:25.320 --> 00:30:26.640
It has a piano solo...

00:30:28.920 --> 00:30:30.600
And the beat drops.

00:30:42.080 --> 00:30:43.160
Tap!

00:30:43.160 --> 00:30:44.560
Tap! Tap!

00:30:44.560 --> 00:30:45.240
Tap! Tap! Tap!

00:31:07.840 --> 00:31:09.240
Not again!

00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:25.480
Middle school... I got tired of gettin'
bullied, so I'm like, okay, I'm a cripple.

00:31:25.480 --> 00:31:28.000
Okay, so I'm gonna get
my fighting skills better.

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:30.040
Joined wrestling.

00:31:30.640 --> 00:31:31.680
I had to wrestle.

00:31:32.560 --> 00:31:35.280
You win some, you loose some.
But you live to fight another day.

00:31:39.400 --> 00:31:40.760
Never give up, Nigger!

00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:50.880
That my friend, is a
professional wrestling match.

00:31:57.800 --> 00:32:01.520
I smile a lot because I try to hide
all the pain that's inside of me.

00:32:01.520 --> 00:32:04.160
That's all I do, every day.

00:32:12.840 --> 00:32:19.080
We do have a moral code. As warped as it may
seem at times, there is a moral code out here.

00:32:20.520 --> 00:32:24.920
It may be a little
anarchical out here...

00:32:24.920 --> 00:32:27.240
Everybody lives by
their own rules.

00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:31.960
As long as it doesn't interfere with
me or affect my life negatively,

00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:34.000
adults can do as they please.

00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:44.760
As skewed as it may seem to the rest of the
world, we have a very strong moral fibre.

00:32:46.080 --> 00:32:50.400
Your neighbor waking you up at 3 o'clock
in the morning when you're sound asleep?

00:32:50.440 --> 00:32:54.480
- Then go live in a residential community
where there's a fuckin' bed-time...

00:32:54.600 --> 00:33:00.000
Oh, I don't give a fuck for tweakers
anymore than I give a FUCK for alcoholics!

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:05.080
- I banned that shit from my cafe!
- I'm not condoning the bad behaviour of people -

00:33:05.080 --> 00:33:09.000
but I'm saying you can't categorize
someone by the substance they do.

00:33:10.520 --> 00:33:12.720
You know what? Yes, I can.

00:33:12.720 --> 00:33:18.320
Because if they know they have a
problem, they have the power to stop it!

00:33:18.320 --> 00:33:20.360
I respect Rob.

00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:24.120
He's tryin' to do well over there.
He started gettin' tired of the tweakers -

00:33:24.120 --> 00:33:26.400
so he started runnin' them out.

00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:30.880
And everybody liked him for that.
You know they stay up all night -

00:33:30.920 --> 00:33:33.720
yellin' and screamin'.
And he was gettin' tired of it.

00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:43.880
We have a big problem with
meth addicts out here.

00:33:44.080 --> 00:33:49.400
Americans call them tweakers, because
they like to tweak with things.

00:33:50.240 --> 00:33:56.080
Stealing things from other people...
They're very desperate drug addicts.

00:33:56.360 --> 00:34:00.880
The police can't do much about that.
And they're not much worried about it either.

00:34:01.280 --> 00:34:04.800
It's very hard to get the
police to respond out here.

00:34:08.960 --> 00:34:12.760
You can't make rules in a
place where there's no rules.

00:34:12.920 --> 00:34:16.960
So you've got the fucking right to wake
me up at 3 in the morning? FUCK YOU!

00:34:17.120 --> 00:34:19.120
You even have a sign in
front of the internet cafe:

00:34:19.320 --> 00:34:21.080
"WE REMEMBER FREEDOM".

00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:24.080
Freedom is not the right
to fuck your neighbors!

00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:28.920
A lot of people didn't like
what they saw here personally,

00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:32.000
and refused to see
the whole picture -

00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:36.920
and they go away thinking that Slab City
is nothing but a bunch of drug addicts.

00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:40.120
And it's not that. It's
an artists community.

00:34:40.280 --> 00:34:45.600
There are unfortunately a lot of
alcoholics and drug users here.

00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:49.960
That's the type of place it is
when you don't have to pay rent.

00:34:50.360 --> 00:34:53.960
You're keepin' us all up over here because you've
got all these fuckin' tweakers over here -

00:34:53.960 --> 00:34:56.200
they're always up
all fuckin' night.

00:34:56.200 --> 00:34:58.040
Well, guess what? You're
gonna fuckin' leave -

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:00.280
if you don't like it, shit's
gonna start happenin'.

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:06.760
Come on, Rob.

00:35:07.840 --> 00:35:09.640
I'll be there in a minute.

00:35:10.680 --> 00:35:13.400
There may sometimes be a lot of yelling
and screaming, but you know what?

00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:18.080
It's better to yell and scream and get it
out than to hold it in and let it build up.

00:35:18.080 --> 00:35:22.840
And... Let it come to the point
where you harm somebody.

00:35:30.840 --> 00:35:35.840
And I understand what you're saying, Rob,
and I apologize, I get it and I agree -

00:35:36.040 --> 00:35:38.360
but how can you take
someone's side,

00:35:38.560 --> 00:35:41.600
and let them come in when it's
not his fuckin' situation -

00:35:41.760 --> 00:35:45.040
and he's done more damage to the
Slabs than anybody fucking here?

00:35:45.680 --> 00:35:50.880
Zack has had, just like a lot of people
here, has had a very fucked up life.

00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:58.760
I have a chance, given time, to show
Zack that there are better ways...

00:36:01.960 --> 00:36:06.920
He could have walked up behind that
guy and put him in the fucking grave.

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:08.600
He didn't.

00:36:08.720 --> 00:36:13.320
The Zack that I met 2.5 years
ago would have just fucking

00:36:13.360 --> 00:36:16.200
taken a club and beaten'
the guy over the head.

00:36:16.280 --> 00:36:19.400
Dude, I'll beat the shit out of you
with both of these coffee thermoses

00:36:19.440 --> 00:36:21.240
and then pour 'em on you.

00:36:22.680 --> 00:36:26.040
I can't say nothin' bad about him.
All the people will be like -

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:27.760
"Oh, he is this, he is that..."

00:36:27.760 --> 00:36:30.160
I've been with Zack ever
since I've been here,

00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:32.320
and I haven't seen him
do nothin' wrong,

00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:34.040
unless it's for a reason.

00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:45.960
You have to respect people out here, or
they're not gonna respect you at all.

00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:50.840
Hey! Look at these douchebags!

00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:54.560
- Hey look, it's a couple of fucks.
- Look at the tapeworms!

00:36:54.640 --> 00:36:58.880
This is an alpha community.
Everybody up here is an alpha.

00:37:01.080 --> 00:37:06.000
And, of course, when two alphas come together,
they're eventually gonna butt heads -

00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:08.240
if they don't have their space.

00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:18.520
But, we do for the most
part live in harmony.

00:37:18.600 --> 00:37:21.160
Rob doesn't like
violence at the cafe.

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:24.280
We don't induce
violence at the cafe.

00:37:24.400 --> 00:37:26.640
We try to stop it
as much as we can.

00:37:28.360 --> 00:37:34.400
In the cafe, the only thing I allow is pot.
Anything harder and they get tossed out.

00:37:34.400 --> 00:37:37.320
I don't even allow
alcohol anymore.

00:37:37.440 --> 00:37:40.800
If they wanna get drunk they
can go somewhere fuckin' else.

00:37:55.120 --> 00:37:59.280
I try not to be negative,
as much as I can.

00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:03.280
When negativity happens, when
there's fights and stuff like that,

00:38:03.320 --> 00:38:04.680
I try to forget those.

00:38:04.720 --> 00:38:08.600
I remember 'em, but I try
not to harbor on them...

00:38:08.800 --> 00:38:12.520
And I try to look at
the chirping of birds.

00:38:14.160 --> 00:38:16.240
The beauty of the desert.

00:38:16.240 --> 00:38:18.720
I try to remember something
beautiful in that situation,

00:38:18.760 --> 00:38:21.000
and that's what
I try to live my life by.

00:38:24.200 --> 00:38:25.440
Sorry Rob.

00:38:28.320 --> 00:38:30.240
I accept your apology.

00:38:33.080 --> 00:38:35.400
None of what you did
was intentional.

00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:03.960
Well, Rob, I gotta tell you...

00:39:03.960 --> 00:39:08.000
He's one of the wisest
men I've met, actually.

00:39:08.360 --> 00:39:11.760
The way he brings himself and the way
he... Like, if somebody gets an argument -

00:39:11.920 --> 00:39:14.960
the way he diffuses it and
the way he words things...

00:39:14.960 --> 00:39:19.320
He loves to conversate with people,
he loves learning about people.

00:39:19.320 --> 00:39:22.440
He just loves people.
Rob's a great person.

00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:34.080
- Hey Steve?
- Yeah?

00:39:34.080 --> 00:39:36.760
I'm just peeking in to see
if Shrieka is in here.

00:39:36.760 --> 00:39:38.040
Yes, she came in.

00:39:38.040 --> 00:39:40.200
- Shrieka did come in?
- Yeah.

00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:43.760
Shrieka? Are you in here, baby?

00:39:46.920 --> 00:39:49.520
No, she's not in here.

00:39:54.840 --> 00:39:55.960
Shrieka!

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:06.200
A lot of us have got our dogs
and we get attached to 'em.

00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:08.840
The cafe's got their own dogs.

00:40:09.200 --> 00:40:12.720
They were puppies that were born
together at the same litter.

00:40:13.200 --> 00:40:18.440
If we didn't have all the dogs, then there
would be a lot of problems around here.

00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:22.400
'Cause whenever I get angry,
all I do is pick up my puppy -

00:40:22.400 --> 00:40:24.960
and look at her face and
all my anger leaves.

00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:26.520
Gentle.

00:40:29.400 --> 00:40:32.920
You teach her gentle.
You teach her gentle, Kato.

00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:35.720
We protect children,
we protect animals.

00:40:36.160 --> 00:40:39.480
We treat our animals better
than we treat ourselves.

00:40:39.640 --> 00:40:45.000
Me and my dog, we usually spend all
day here with nobody comin' around.

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:50.000
I enjoy the solitude of just being
alone and being able to relax.

00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:53.760
Yeah, I love it out here.
I just love it.

00:41:01.480 --> 00:41:07.480
If I had one wish, I wish I
could find me a nice woman.

00:41:07.480 --> 00:41:10.280
I even posted it
online, on Facebook:

00:41:10.280 --> 00:41:13.960
"I'm looking for a nice
woman, to stay with me -

00:41:13.960 --> 00:41:15.600
do the cookin' and cleanin' -

00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:17.400
do my laundry..."

00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:19.040
And everybody said:
"You want a maid -

00:41:19.120 --> 00:41:21.520
you don't want a fuckin' wife!"

00:41:22.640 --> 00:41:24.800
Tomorrow's my birthday.

00:41:24.800 --> 00:41:27.240
I'm gonna be 65 years old.

00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:34.400
It'd be nice to settle down a little bit.
And it'd be nice to stay with a woman.

00:41:34.400 --> 00:41:36.400
Share that with, you know.

00:41:40.880 --> 00:41:43.240
And now I'm gettin' all
sentimental and shit.

00:41:51.760 --> 00:41:53.160
Shrieka?

00:41:58.240 --> 00:41:59.640
Shrieka?

00:42:08.440 --> 00:42:11.480
You get to know the animals,
you get to know them by name.

00:42:11.480 --> 00:42:15.160
They'll run out, they'll talk to you,
they'll say hi to you in the mornings -

00:42:15.360 --> 00:42:18.800
and then they go on to
their journey of the day.

00:42:19.240 --> 00:42:22.720
There you are, baby!
Hi! Come here!

00:42:23.320 --> 00:42:24.440
Come on!

00:42:24.800 --> 00:42:26.920
You had me worried, baby.

00:42:26.920 --> 00:42:28.000
Come on up!

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:32.000
Hi Gator.

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:35.200
Yes, hi Gator.

00:42:37.920 --> 00:42:40.760
You had me worried, baby.

00:42:41.200 --> 00:42:45.480
Well then, I gotta avoid the
police until April 30th.

00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:46.920
Is it traffic tickets?

00:42:47.720 --> 00:42:51.320
It's traffic court, it's not a ticket,
Bro, it's a fuckin' evading arrest...

00:42:52.560 --> 00:42:56.600
- You was evading arrest?
- I destroyed a cop car with a F-350.

00:42:56.600 --> 00:42:58.960
Hey! Fuck off!

00:42:59.880 --> 00:43:04.040
You're gonna come play next to me right
when I'm drinking coffee, piss off! Go!

00:43:04.960 --> 00:43:05.760
GO!

00:43:06.920 --> 00:43:08.240
Go, motherfucker!

00:43:08.240 --> 00:43:13.040
And that's how I got caught up and that's why
I'm going through all this stupid bullshit now.

00:43:13.080 --> 00:43:16.240
Today is my brother Zack's
birthday and he is turning 19 -

00:43:16.280 --> 00:43:19.840
and we're goin' to celebrate
it by doin' everything

00:43:19.840 --> 00:43:22.320
under the sun that can
not get us in trouble...

00:43:23.640 --> 00:43:26.360
While still having fun
at the same time.

00:43:26.360 --> 00:43:31.120
I at least have to not go to
jail until after my birthday.

00:43:49.320 --> 00:43:52.320
I will eventually,
one day, be leaving.

00:43:52.320 --> 00:43:56.000
There will come a day when I won't
be able to go up on the roof anymore,

00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:57.720
to move the panels around.

00:44:11.320 --> 00:44:14.600
- Hey Zack? You wanna come here?
- Yo?

00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:18.640
Yeah, come here. I need you
to fix this a little bit.

00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:23.680
We've got this back and we can't
have the cord, and also...

00:44:26.800 --> 00:44:34.640
And when that day comes, that will
definitely be the day that I leave.

00:44:34.640 --> 00:44:39.760
Who knows? It may be sooner
but, right now, this is home.

00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:59.640
And we're goin' to get
so hammered tonight.

00:44:59.760 --> 00:45:02.360
I don't know what we're doin', but
we're gonna have fun tonight.

00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:04.560
We are at The Range,
a very special place...

00:45:04.880 --> 00:45:12.480
I advise everybody to come to
The Range at Slab City. Please.

00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:28.480
Saturdays, like tonight, is one
of the biggest nights of the week,

00:45:28.520 --> 00:45:32.640
because we all gather up on the stage
that was set up by Builder Bill -

00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.720
and it's called The Range.

00:45:36.280 --> 00:45:41.280
That's when the alcohol flows through and I
do have my good times on Saturday nights.

00:45:41.280 --> 00:45:42.960
Sundays are my day off.

00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:47.080
I don't do nothin'. Somebody comes over, wants
somethin' done, I'll tell them I'll do it on Monday,

00:45:47.080 --> 00:45:49.160
because I've usually
got a hangover.

00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:53.840
It's fantastic, I just go out there
and dance, dance my heart out.

00:45:53.840 --> 00:45:58.920
And I'm better when I come back on Sunday.
A whole better person again.

00:46:51.680 --> 00:46:54.080
Yeah, we work hard and we
play hard out here too.

00:46:54.880 --> 00:46:58.280
Different tones, different
pitches, different instruments.

00:46:58.360 --> 00:47:05.680
I've seen all the way from a cello to a
flute to harmonica playing the blues -

00:47:05.800 --> 00:47:10.320
up there on that Range.
It is a range of music.

00:47:59.720 --> 00:48:03.480
I may go down to listen
to a new musician

00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:07.960
for half an hour to an hour,
but that's pretty much it.

00:48:08.040 --> 00:48:11.000
This place keeps me pretty busy
and by the time that's goin' on,

00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:14.920
I'm pretty tired and just
wanna sit back and relax.

00:48:22.120 --> 00:48:24.120
Dream on!

00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:28.880
Thanks.

00:49:03.120 --> 00:49:07.440
I'm as human as everybody else,
I make my stupid mistakes.

00:49:09.960 --> 00:49:14.840
But I do tend to be
self-reflective.

00:49:15.240 --> 00:49:17.360
Think about...

00:49:17.360 --> 00:49:22.920
Geez, what did I just do?
What I wanna really do?

00:49:35.600 --> 00:49:40.080
Don't stop learning,
don't stop growing...

00:49:41.800 --> 00:49:46.600
Work harder each day to be a better
person than you were yesterday.

00:49:46.640 --> 00:49:49.200
And never rest on your laurels.

00:49:55.880 --> 00:50:02.520
For your own personal growth,
you need to constantly learn.

00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:10.800
That's the mistake too many people make,
is resting on their accomplishments.

00:50:10.880 --> 00:50:13.480
You gotta keep doing
something new.

00:50:24.080 --> 00:50:28.560
My mother worked for the
same employer for 32 years.

00:50:28.720 --> 00:50:34.880
My sister is months away from putting in
her 30th year with a single employer.

00:50:34.920 --> 00:50:36.800
Couldn't do it!

00:50:37.960 --> 00:50:41.240
Maybe if I was an
astronaut for NASA, yes.

00:50:42.600 --> 00:50:46.080
I plan on going to the
moon before I die.

00:51:37.880 --> 00:51:42.520
They keep kicking me off the private
network and it's really pissing me off.

00:51:42.640 --> 00:51:44.880
So before you leave we definitely
have to take care of the internet -

00:51:44.920 --> 00:51:47.920
and me getting on and
off without complications.

00:51:47.960 --> 00:51:49.040
Yeah.

